WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.100
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.298
<v Examiner>Explain why discharge planning starts on admission,

3
00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:09.687
<v Examiner>and describe what a nurse would include in a patient's discharge plan.

4
00:00:10.137 --> 00:00:11.049
Explain first.

5
00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:16.585
Discharge planning starts on admission because it's an interdisciplinary process that

6
00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:18.214
takes time to coordinate,

7
00:00:18.214 --> 00:00:23.815
and its aim is continuity of care and a smooth transition home or to the next service.

8
00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:27.983
Starting early reduces readmissions, reduces the length of stay,

9
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:30.914
and reduces the need for community follow-up.

10
00:00:30.914 --> 00:00:32.542
The nurse coordinates it,

11
00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:36.776
and is often the last point of contact before the patient leaves.

12
00:00:36.776 --> 00:00:42.573
The process runs like the nursing process: assess, plan and prepare, implement, evaluate.

13
00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:44.654
Now describe what goes in.

14
00:00:44.654 --> 00:00:45.784
From Lisa's slide.

15
00:00:45.784 --> 00:00:48.796
The mode of discharge: how they're getting home.

16
00:00:48.796 --> 00:00:52.874
Self-care: their medicines, diet, wound care and pain management.

17
00:00:52.874 --> 00:00:54.819
Equipment, and how it's set up.

18
00:00:54.819 --> 00:00:56.263
Follow-up appointments.

19
00:00:56.263 --> 00:00:59.212
Permitted activities, like lifting and driving.

20
00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:02.036
Warning signs, and what to do if they happen.

21
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.353
And health promotion.

22
00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:08.701
And the step people forget: make sure the patient and their family understand the plan,

23
00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:12.079
agree with it, and have everything they need before they go.

24
00:01:12.079 --> 00:01:13.937
Teach-back is how you check that.

25
00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:18.071
Discharge planning starts at admission: interdisciplinary,

26
00:01:18.071 --> 00:01:23.152
for continuity and a smooth transition; it cuts readmissions and length of stay.

27
00:01:23.152 --> 00:01:24.296
Nurse coordinates.

28
00:01:24.296 --> 00:01:26.455
Assess, plan, implement, evaluate.

29
00:01:26.455 --> 00:01:31.537
Include: how they get home, medicines, diet, wounds, pain, equipment, follow-up,

30
00:01:31.537 --> 00:01:34.903
lifting and driving, warning signs, health promotion.

31
00:01:34.903 --> 00:01:36.936
Check they understand and agree.
